# Data Modeling — Star Schema

## 1. Overview

The Gold layer of the IPL data engineering pipeline uses dimensional data modeling to organize transformed cricket data for analytics and reporting.

The model follows a Star Schema consisting of dimension tables and fact tables.

The purpose of the model is to separate descriptive attributes from measurable business events and provide an analytics-ready structure for Power BI.

---

## 2. Data Modeling Flow

```text
CricAPI
   ↓
Bronze
match_raw
   ↓
Silver
silver_innings
silver_match_innings
   ↓
Gold
Dimension Tables + Fact Tables
   ↓
Power BI
3. Star Schema

The Gold layer is organized around fact tables connected to related dimension tables.

Conceptually:

              dim_date
                 |
                 |
dim_team ─── fact_match ─── dim_venue
                 |
                 |
            dim_player

The dimensions provide descriptive context, while fact tables contain measurable cricket performance data.

4. Dimension Tables

The project uses dimension tables to store descriptive attributes used for analysis.

Examples include:

dim_date

Stores date-related attributes used for time-based analysis.

Possible analytical attributes include:

Date
Year
Month
Season
dim_team

Stores team-related descriptive attributes.

Used for:

Team analysis
Match participation
Team performance reporting
dim_venue

Stores venue-related attributes.

Used for:

Venue analysis
Match location reporting
Venue-level performance analysis
dim_player

Stores player-related attributes used for player performance analysis.

5. Fact Tables

Fact tables contain measurable events and performance metrics.

The Gold layer is designed to support analytical questions such as:

How many runs were scored?
How many wickets were taken?
Which team won a match?
How did a player perform?
What was the performance at a particular venue?
How did performance change across seasons?
6. Dimension and Fact Relationships

The Star Schema allows fact records to be analyzed using different dimensions.

For example:

Fact Performance
      |
      +── Team
      |
      +── Player
      |
      +── Date
      |
      +── Venue

This structure makes it easier for reporting tools to filter and aggregate cricket performance data.

7. SCD Type 2

Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2 is used where historical changes to dimension attributes need to be preserved.

Instead of overwriting an existing dimension record, a new version of the record is created when the tracked attribute changes.

Conceptually:

Player / Team Attribute
        ↓
Existing Record
        ↓
Attribute Changes
        ↓
Close Previous Version
        ↓
Insert New Version

A Type 2 implementation can use fields such as:

effective_start_date
effective_end_date
is_current

This allows historical versions to remain available for analysis.

8. Why Star Schema?

The Star Schema provides:

Clear separation between facts and dimensions
Simpler analytical queries
Consistent dimensions for reporting
Easier aggregation of performance metrics
A business-friendly structure for Power BI
Support for historical dimension analysis through SCD Type 2
9. Gold Layer Purpose

The Gold layer provides analytics-ready datasets for downstream reporting.

The design follows the principle:

Bronze = Raw
Silver = Clean and Validated
Gold   = Business / Analytics Ready

The Gold layer should be the primary source for downstream BI reporting rather than directly querying Bronze or raw API data.

